# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# GitHub Token Configuration
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Option 1: Single token (simplest, 5000 req/hr)
GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=ghp_your_token_here

# Option 2: Multi-token rotation pool (recommended, N × 5000 req/hr)
# Comma-separated; automatically picks the token with the most remaining quota
# GITHUB_TOKENS=ghp_alice_token,ghp_bob_token,ghp_carol_token
#
# ⚠️ Important: Multiple tokens from the same GitHub account share a single 5000/hr quota!
# Tokens in the pool must come from different GitHub accounts to stack quotas.
# Example: 3 team members each contribute 1 token = 3 × 5000 = 15000 req/hr
#
# Priority: GITHUB_TOKENS > GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN > GITHUB_TOKEN

# How to get a token:
#   1. https://github.com/settings/tokens
#   2. Recommended: Fine-grained token (more secure):
#      - "Generate new token" → "Fine-grained personal access token"
#      - Repository access: Public Repositories (read-only)
#      - Permissions → Repository: Issues (Read-only), Pull requests (Read-only)
#      - Recommended expiration: 90 days
#   3. Or Classic token (simpler):
#      - "Generate new token (classic)"
#      - Check public_repo
#   4. For private repos (e.g. ROCm/aiter): requires repo scope (classic) or full permissions for the repo (fine-grained)

# ⚠️ Security notes:
# - Run chmod 600 .env after creating this file
# - This file is excluded by .gitignore; never commit it to Git
# - Tokens leaked to public repos will be automatically revoked by GitHub

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Path overrides (optional, usually no changes needed)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SIGNALS_DB_PATH=data/signals.db
# CACHE_DIR=data/cache
# CONFIG_PATH=config/sources.yaml
